  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Page No.# 1/5 vs The State Of Assam on 9 December, 2024 Page No.# 1 Gahc010107822010 2024:Gau-As:12584 The Gauhati High Court (High Court Of Assam, Nagaland, Mizoram And Arunachal Pradesh) Case No. : Crl.Rev.P./498/2010 Sri Gopi Agarwala and Anr S/O Sri Nathmal Agarwala 2: Sri Nathmal Agarwala Proprietor Of M/S Mira Bhandar Hospital Road Dhekiajuli Town Mouza and P.S. Dhekiajuli Dist. Sonitpur Assam Versus The State Of Assam Advocate for the Petitioner : Mr. T C Khatri, Mr. P Mahanta,Mr.S K Jain Advocate for the Respondent : , ,Pp, Assam Before Hon'Ble Mr Justice Arun Dev Choudhury For the Petitioner : Mr. S. K. Jain, Advocate. For the Respondents : Mr. B. Sarma, App. Date of Hearing : 09.12.2024 Page No.# 2/5 Page No.# 1/5 vs The State Of Assam on 9 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/122656016/ 1 Date of Judgement : 09.12.2024 Judgment & Order (Oral) 1.",
    "facts": "2. The present criminal revision petition under Section 397/401 read with Section 482 of Cr.P.C., 1973 is filed assailing a Judgment and Order dated 15.10.1998 passed by the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Sonitpur, Tazpur in C.R. Case No. 1589/1994, whereby the accused petitioners were convicted under Section 7/16 of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (hereinafter referred to as Act, 1954) and petitioners were sentenced to undergo Simple Imprisonment for 6 (six) months each and to pay a fine of Rs. 1,000/- each and in default to pay fine, Simple Imprisonment for another 1 (one) month. However, in terms of Section 52 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred to as Act, 2006), the punishment prescribed is Page No.# 3/5 now only fine upto Rs. 3 lakhs and therefore he submits that the petitioners should also get benefit of the aforesaid principle of law laid down by the Hon'ble Apex Court. The basic allegation in the complaint is to the effect that as per the Public Analyst Report the sample of Iodised Salt does not conform to the standard. Such materials were seized from the possession of the petitioners. Accordingly, two petitioners were prosecuted.",
    "arguments": "In view of the aforesaid principle of law laid down by the Hon'ble Apex Court, the learned counsel for the petitioners argues that now the sentence is required to be modified as per Section 52 of the Act, 2006."
  },
